                     1 S.C.R. 402; Lizotte v. Aviva Insurance Company of Canada, 2016 SCC 52, [2016] 2 S.C.R. 521; The Queen v. Laliberté (1877), 1 S.C.R. 117; R. v. J.J., <b>2022 SCC 28</b>, [2022] 2 S.C.R. 3; R. v. Harrer, [1995] 3 S.C.R. 562; R. v. Demers, 2004 SCC 46, [2004] 2 S.C.R. 489; R. v. Lyttle, 2004 SCC 5, [2004] 1 S.C.R. 193; R. v. &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp; 117, at p. 140, per Ritchie J.; Roberts, at p. 545; Woltucky, at pp. 46-47; Steele, at pp. 172-73 and 181; R. v. J.J., <b>2022 SCC 28</b>, [2022] 2 S.C.R. 3, at paras. 113-14). This right guarantees the accused a fair opportunity to challenge the evidence and present a defence (R. v. Harrer, [1995] 3 S.C.R. 562, at para. 13). 
                </p>
